    "https://mwsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/4425": {
      "title": "Missouri Western State University Portal | Financial Aid Coordinator",
      "description": "Missouri Western State University Portal | Financial Aid Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Financial Aid Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications will be reviewed as received and continue until position is filled. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Financial Aid Coordinator Job Description The Financial Aid Coordinator performs technical specialized duties in the administration of student financial assistance programs, following all relevant federal regulations and institutional policies. ESSENTIAL DUTIES : Provide excellent customer service to all applicants, their families, and members of the community. Assist students and prospective students with completing financial aid applications and provide guidance in locating additional financial resources Compare FAFSA application with documentation collected from students; identify and resolve discrepant information; utilize federal data systems to update student records. Retrieve ISIR files from the Department of Education; code and format files into Banner, batch post, and post tracking requirements based on the ISIR file. Award, document, and track departmental and Foundation scholarships. Award each student’s federal financial aid for each semester and notify the students of what financial aid they will be receiving for the upcoming semester. Perform other duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Expert knowledge of all federal, state, and institutional aid programs, including all applicable regulations and policies. Ability to provide accurate information to students and families based on established laws and policies. Knowledge of tax laws, and the ability to assist students and families with the FAFSA application and the verification process. Knowledge of financial aid websites. Proficient in Microsoft Office programs and other general office equipment. Ability to learn new computer software. Organized thinker with exceptional attention to detail. Excellent communication skills, both verbally and in writing. Strong customer service skills. Ability to effectively organize and prioritize work as well as concentrate on multiple tasks simultaneously Required Qualifications High School diploma or GED One to three years of financial aid, customer service, or related experience sufficient to successfully perform the essential duties of the job. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree in Accounting, Finance, Business, or a related field is preferred. Physical Demands General office conditions. Exposed to moderate noise levels. Required to use close vision and be able to focus. Regularly required to talk and hear; frequently required to sit, stand, and bend at the knee and waist, and walk. Must be able to have repetitive wrist, hand and/or finger movement to type and work on computer. Must have finger dexterity and hand-eye coordination to work on computer, telephone, and related office equipment. Regular attendance is a necessary and essential function. FLSA Non-Exempt Additional Demands The Financial Aid Coordinator may assist other coordinators with processes related to the administration of scholarships, grants, loans, and third party aid. Continual participation in compliance webinars, conferences, and training is required to successfully perform job duties. Hours of Work Monday-Friday; 8:00 am-4:30 pm Posting Detail Information Posting Number S855P Open Date 07/31/2026 Priority Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ * Are you currently or have you ever been, NASFAA Certified? yes No * What is your highest level of education attained? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) Professional References (3-5 with contact information) Optional Documents Missouri Western State University 4525 Downs Drive, St. Joseph, MO 64507 An equal opportunity/affirmative action institution. © 2019 Missouri Western State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
