    "https://mwsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/4357": {
      "title": "Missouri Western State University Portal",
      "description": "Missouri Western State University Portal | Groundskeeper/Events Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Groundskeeper/Events Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin upon receipt and will continue until position is filled. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Groundskeeper/Events Job Description The Groundskeeper for Missouri Western State University joins a team of individuals who take pride in caring for the University property. The Groundskeeper performs maintenance and upkeep of the beautiful university grounds, landscaping, parking lots, streets, and athletic fields. Enjoy a great schedule and excellent benefits including generous paid time off, retirement, insurance and paid tuition for employee and/or dependents. ESSENTIAL DUTIES : Maintains university grounds, parking lots, streets, and athletic fields by mowing, landscaping, trimming, planting, watering, fertilizing, and patching with the aid of grounds maintenance equipment; including tractors, backhoes, skid loaders, dump trucks, and snow removal equipment. Performs routine maintenance and repair on grounds equipment. Picks up trash on campus grounds and streets and empties exterior campus waste receptacles. Assists with moving equipment, materials, supplies, furnishings, etc. for departments and university events. Assists in the installation of underground utilities, such as sprinkler systems, water, gas, sewer, and electrical lines. Measures and paints athletic fields for games and events and performs maintenance on sprinkler systems. Performs other duties of a similar nature or level. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Care and maintenance of turf, trees and flowers Operation and maintenance of grounds equipment Safe operation of mowers, tractors, backhoes, skid loaders, and dump trucks Communication as applied to interaction with coworkers, supervisors, administrators, and the general public Required Qualifications High School Diploma or GED Three years of groundskeeping experience. Candidate must have experience in lawn care, landscaping, and snow removal. Must be experienced in operating heavy equipment, tractor, trucks, and skid loader. Ability to work outside in all weather conditions. Able to work on call nights and weekends for emergency call in work. Ability to frequently lift 50 pounds. Ability to stand and walk on hard or uneven surfaces. Candidate must have reliable transportation and a valid driver’s license, preferably a Class E license, or willing to obtain within 90 days. Candidate must be safety minded and have the ability to show up to work on time, consistently. Preferred Qualifications Experience in horticulture, farming and landscaping. State chemical applicator’s license Physical Demands Very Heavy Work Exerting in excess of 50 pounds of force frequently, and/or in excess of 20 pounds of force constantly to move objects. Incumbents may be subjected to moving mechanical parts, electrical currents, vibrations, fumes, odors, dusts, gases, poor ventilation, chemicals, oils, extreme temperatures, inadequate lighting, work space restrictions, intense noises, and travel. FLSA Non-Exempt Additional Demands Some nights, weekends and holidays required. OT as required. Hours of Work M-F 7am-3:30pm Posting Detail Information Posting Number S849P Open Date 07/20/2026 Priority Deadline 07/27/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ * Are you available to work in the evening (6 pm to 10 pm)? Yes No * Are you available to work weekends? Yes No * Do you have a valid current driver's license? Yes No * Do you have a high school diploma or GED? Yes No * How many years of experience do you have operating heavy equipment? (tractor, trucks, skid loader) (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Professional References (3-5 with contact information) Optional Documents Transcripts (unofficial) Missouri Western State University 4525 Downs Drive, St. Joseph, MO 64507 An equal opportunity/affirmative action institution. © 2019 Missouri Western State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
