      "title": "Missouri Western State University Portal",
      "description": "Missouri Western State University Portal | Accountant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Accountant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Accountant Job Description The Office of Accounting Services at Missouri Western State University (MoWest) is seeking applications for the position of Accountant as MoWest looks to improve its business processes for its new strategic plan. The Accountant will be responsible for the management and reporting of financial information. Their duties include preparing financial statements, performing bookkeeping, examining and analyzing the University’s accounts, and ensuring compliance with GASB financial reporting and generally accepted accounting principles ( GAAP ). Accounting Services is part of the Finance and Administration division of MoWest and works closely with the office(s) of Budget, Purchasing, and Student Financial Services. ESSENTIAL DUTIES Assigned a primary responsibility for one or more of the following activities: bank deposits, accounts payable, accounts receivable, fixed assets, leases, grants and federal funds, and/or debt management. Prepare and examine financial records, ensuring records are accurate and complete. Perform day-to-day transactions while ensuring established policies and procedures are followed. Posting financial transactions, including receivables and payables, using appropriate software. Reconcile accounts to appropriate ledgers and statements; report and correct discrepancies. Prepare third party billings and track payments for accuracy. Regular reconciliation of asset and liability accounts. Produce analysis for internal and external audit activities. Perform allocations and journal entries. Filing and remitting taxes and other reporting obligations. Assists other departments with overall inquiries regarding revenues and expenditures. Produce reports with accuracy and completeness. Performs other related duties as assigned. KNOWLEDGE , SKILLS & ABILITIES Knowledge of and ability to adhere to GAAP . Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Proficient in Microsoft Office Excel, Word and similar software. Communication, as applied to interaction with coworkers, supervisors, the general public, etc., is sufficient to exchange or convey information and to receive work direction. Required Qualifications Associate’s degree in accounting, finance, or related discipline One (1) year of accounting experience Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in accounting, finance, or related discipline 2-3 years of accounting experience Fund or management accounting experience Physical Demands Sedentary Work Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects, including the human body. Sedentary work involves sitting most of the time. Jobs are sedentary if walking and standing are required only occasionally and all other sedentary criteria are met FLSA Exempt Additional Demands Hours of Work M-F 8am-4:30pm Posting Detail Information Posting Number S853P Open Date 07/22/2026 Priority Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ * What is your highest level of education attained? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) Professional References (3-5 with contact information) Optional Documents Missouri Western State University 4525 Downs Drive, St. Joseph, MO 64507 An equal opportunity/affirmative action institution. © 2019 Missouri Western State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes 