    "https://mwsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/4389": {
      "title": "Missouri Western State University Portal | Administrative Assistant",
      "description": "Missouri Western State University Portal | Administrative Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Assistant Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Interviews will begin as applications are received and continue until position is filled. Posting Details Position Information Position Title Administrative Assistant Job Description The Administrative Assistant assists in the daily operational management of a department, including budgeting, customer service, and administrative support duties. Essential Duties: Serves as initial contact, answers telephones, emails, assesses and responds to inquiries, provides appropriate information and direction, scheduling classroom or event space, processes mail and packages. Prepares and reviews reports, forms, and documents; ensures compliance with policies and campus procedures; maintains web pages; schedules and prepares for meetings and/or special events. Processes purchase orders and remittance vouchers, maintains office supplies, and collects and deposits miscellaneous monies. Assigns and supervises the work of student employees. Serves as operational liaison to other departments, campus, and community Assists with the development and oversight of budget and financial information, such as maintaining balances, researching discrepancies, and preparing reports and recommendations. Assists in the coordination and publicity of departmental activities and events, including the design of brochures, newsletters, or invitations. Performs other duties of a similar nature or level. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Office principles and practices Budgeting principles Basic mathematics Customer service Computer and basic office equipment Software applications (some positions require knowledge of specific operating system and HTML ) Grammar and writing formats Organizational skills Problem solving Ability to multitask with attention to detail Research, preparation, and analysis of data Communication as applied to interaction with students, coworkers, supervisor and the general public Required Qualifications High School diploma or GED ; and One year of specialized training in administrative support or a related field; and Three years of administrative support or related office experience Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands Sedentary Work Exerting up to 10 pounds of force occasionally and/or a negligible amount of force frequently or constantly to lift, carry, push, pull or otherwise move objects, including the human body. Sedentary work involves sitting most of the time. Jobs are sedentary if walking and standing are required only occasionally and all other sedentary criteria are met. FLSA Non-Exempt Additional Demands Some departments may require occasional night or evening work Hours of Work Monday – Friday 8am – 4:30pm Posting Detail Information Posting Number S848P Open Date 07/08/2026 Priority Deadline 07/15/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Do you have a high school diploma or GED? Yes No * How  many years of Administrative support experience do you have? 0-2 3-5 6-9 10 or more * Do you have significant experience with the following applications? Word Excel PowerPoint Visio Most of the above All of the above Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) Professional References (3-5 with contact information) Optional Documents Missouri Western State University 4525 Downs Drive, St. Joseph, MO 64507 An equal opportunity/affirmative action institution. © 2019 Missouri Western State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://mwsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/4416": {
      "title": "Missouri Western State University Portal",
      "description": "Missouri Western State University Portal | Academic Advisor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Academic Advisor Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Academic Advisor Job Description The Academic Advisor plays a vital role in supporting student success by providing comprehensive and proactive student-centered academic advising to new freshmen, undecided transfer students, at-risk students, and other designated student populations. This position empowers students to make informed academic decisions, develop educational plans, and successfully navigate university policies, procedures, and resources. Through individualized advising, registration support, and campus collaboration, this position promotes student success, retention, and timely degree completion while fostering an inclusive and supporting learning environment. ESSENTIAL DUTIES : Advises undecided, high risk, new freshmen, undecided transfer students, and other special populations Monitors and advises students to ensure satisfactory grades and GPA requirements, students understand academic policies, as well as course planning/registration Develops workshops for a variety of student groups; prepares and makes presentations for Registration Days, Griffon Edge and other on –campus groups Maintains professional contacts and an awareness of best practices and standards in the advising field; stays current with relevant research Stays abreast of changing institutional information including new programs, course changes, important dates, costs, and updates in university-wide initiatives and policies Understands the institution’s interpretation of FERPA rules for the release of student information to faculty, parents, students, etc. Available to meet with students in person or virtually via Zoom throughout the year, through scheduled 1-on-1 appointments, group advising sessions, or drop-in advising Establishes and maintains ongoing contact with students through a variety of communication methods, including telephone, email, Zoom, and social media platforms Advise during new student registration programs Accurately document advisement and student meeting details Serve on campus committees, as needed Performs other duties of a similar nature or level Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of advising theory and best practices in academic advisement Challenges of entering freshman and transfer students and effective retention strategies Teaching techniques and strategies Effective advising techniques with special populations Ability to research and write reports Strong organizational skills (maintaining accurate files), and (verbal and written) communication skills Ability to work collaboratively with campus constituents Computer application skills Knowledge of Banner and DegreeWorks preferred Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Education, Advising or related field. Preferred Qualifications Two years postsecondary education advisement experience. Physical Demands Sedentary Work: Exerting up to 10 pounds FLSA Exempt Additional Demands Hours of Work Monday-Friday 8:00 am – 4:30 pm Posting Detail Information Posting Number S856P Open Date 08/11/2026 Priority Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ * What is your Philosophy for serving students? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have prior experience in Higher Education? Yes No * What is your highest level of education attained? (Open Ended Question) Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) Professional References (3-5 with contact information) Optional Documents Missouri Western State University 4525 Downs Drive, St. Joseph, MO 64507 An equal opportunity/affirmative action institution. © 2019 Missouri Western State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://mwsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/4434": {
      "title": "Missouri Western State University Portal | Technical Director: Potter Hall Theater",
      "description": "Missouri Western State University Portal | Technical Director: Potter Hall Theater Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Technical Director: Potter Hall Theater Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Technical Director: Potter Hall Theater Job Description Missouri Western State University School of Fine Arts is seeking an experienced Technical Director to manage all technical operations for musical performances and events in Potter Theater. This is a yearly contract position (subject to budget constraints and annual renewal) beginning in August 2026 . The Technical Director will be responsible for the safe, professional, and efficient setup, operation, and strike of lighting, sound, rigging, and stage elements for concerts, recitals, choral performances, symphonic winds, and other large-ensemble music events. Key Responsibilities Lead all technical aspects of music events in Potter Theater, including lighting design and operation, sound reinforcement, stage rigging, concert shell placement, and full stage setup/teardown. Collaborate closely with music faculty, ensemble directors, and performers to realize their artistic vision safely and effectively. Oversee the safe operation of the theater’s lighting system, sound equipment, rigging points, and stage elements, including the permanently locked orchestra pit. Ensure all setups meet safety standards, best practices, and university policies for live performance venues. Recruit, train, and supervise student crew members and volunteers for each event. Coordinate with university facilities staff on any needed maintenance or repairs to technical systems. Arrive in advance for load-in and remain until full strike and reset is complete for each event. Required Qualifications Minimum 2–3 years of professional experience in theatrical technical direction, lighting, sound, or stage management. Strong working knowledge of theatrical lighting consoles, sound reinforcement systems, and stage rigging. Experience supporting live music performances and large ensembles (preferred). Demonstrated commitment to safety and best practices in a performance venue. Ability to work flexible hours, including evenings and weekends. Ability to lift up to 50 lbs and work at heights when necessary. Reliable transportation required. Preferred Qualifications Physical Demands FLSA Non-Exempt Additional Demands Nights and weekends as needed for performances in the theater. Hours of Work Posting Detail Information Posting Number S858P Open Date 08/18/2026 Priority Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ Are you available to work in the evening (6 pm to 10 pm)? Yes No Are you available to work weekends? Yes No Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) Professional References (3-5 with contact information) Optional Documents Missouri Western State University 4525 Downs Drive, St. Joseph, MO 64507 An equal opportunity/affirmative action institution. © 2019 Missouri Western State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://mwsu.peopleadmin.com/postings/4447": {
      "title": "Missouri Western State University Portal | Campus Visits and Events Coordinator",
      "description": "Missouri Western State University Portal | Campus Visits and Events Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Campus Visits and Events Coordinator Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Position Information Position Title Campus Visits and Events Coordinator Job Description The Campus Visits and Events Coordinator is responsible for creating and overseeing a welcoming, engaging, and impactful campus visit experience for prospective students, families, counselors, and community partners. This position provides leadership for campus visit programming and events, including individual and group visits, campus visit days, tours, and related experiences. The Coordinator works collaboratively with campus partners and student ambassadors to ensure visitors receive a consistent and positive experience that reflects the Missouri Western community and supports the university’s enrollment and student recruitment goals. Essential Job Functions Serves as the primary point of contact and provides leadership for campus visits and experiences throughout the year, ensuring programs are welcoming, engaging, and aligned with university enrollment goals. Plans, coordinates, and oversees the logistics and execution of undergraduate enrollment events, working collaboratively with campus partners to ensure facilities, audiovisual needs, catering, scheduling, CRM updates, and other event requirements are effectively managed. Assists the Director and campus partners to develop and deliver Griffon Orientation (GO) programs that provide engaging and meaningful on-campus experiences for prospective students and their families. Builds and maintains strong partnerships with faculty and staff to coordinate individualized experiences for prospective students, ensuring campus connections are purposeful, well-organized, and reflective of the university’s commitment to student success. Leads the planning and execution of group tours, Saturday tours, Athletic tours, Griffon Experience events, and other campus visit programs, ensuring each experience is organized, informative, and welcoming for prospective students and families. Recruits, trains, supervises, and develops student ambassadors to serve as knowledgeable and welcoming representatives of Missouri Western. Provides leadership and guidance to ensure ambassadors are prepared to support campus visits, the department front desk, and university main phone coverage. Oversees the visitor experience from initial contact through follow-up, maintaining accurate campus visit data and developing meaningful follow-up strategies that strengthen engagement and support prospective students throughout the enrollment process. Continuously evaluates campus visit and event experiences, identifies opportunities for improvement, and collaborates with campus partners to enhance programs and strengthen their contribution to student recruitment and enrollment. Performs other related duties as assigned. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong organizational and time management skills Excellent written and oral communication skills Ability to work independently and as part of a team Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree Preferred Qualifications One year of experience in event management Experience in higher education, specifically admissions or student affairs Physical Demands Light Work Exerting up to 20 pounds of force occasionally, and/or up to 10 pounds of force frequently, and/or negligible amount of force constantly to move objects. If the use of arm and/or leg controls requires exertion of forces greater than that for Sedentary Work and the worker sits most of the time, the job is rated for Light Work FLSA Exempt Additional Demands Night and weekend work is required. Hours of Work Posting Detail Information Posting Number S859P Open Date 08/28/2026 Priority Deadline Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have a bachelor's degree? Yes No Are you available to work in the evening (6 pm to 10 pm)? Yes No Are you available to work weekends? Yes No How many years of experience do you have in this type of position? 0-1 1-3 3-5 5-7 7+ Documents Needed To Apply Required Documents Resume Cover Letter Transcripts (unofficial) Professional References (3-5 with contact information) Optional Documents Missouri Western State University 4525 Downs Drive, St. Joseph, MO 64507 An equal opportunity/affirmative action institution. © 2019 Missouri Western State University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    }
